        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: G. D. Spradlin, Marlon Brando, Al Pacino, Charlton Heston, George C. Scott, Johnny Depp\n- Films: A Streetcar Named Desire, On the Waterfront, The Godfather, Viva Zapata!, Sayonara\n- Topics: acting credits, film performances, awards\n\nFacts:\n- Marlon Brando starred in the 1951 film \"A Streetcar Named Desire.\"\n- Marlon Brando won an Academy Award for playing Terry Malloy in \"On the Waterfront\" (1954).\n- \"Sayonara\" is a 1957 Technicolor American film starring Marlon Brando in Technirama.\n- Marlon Brando won an Academy Award for playing Vito Corleone in \"The Godfather\" (1972).\n- G. D. Spradlin is credited in over 70 television and film productions.\n- G. D. Spradlin performed alongside actors including Marlon Brando, Al Pacino, Charlton Heston, George C. Scott, and Johnny Depp.",
